<p>This route is used mostly by travellers connecting onward by rail — catching an AVE high-speed service south to Toledo, Seville, and Córdoba, or east to Valencia and Alicante, sometimes on the very same day as an international flight. Landing with a train to catch adds a layer of pressure that a private, pre-booked transfer is built to remove: the car and driver are arranged before you even board, and you can <a href="/get-a-quote/">get a quote</a> for the fixed fare well ahead of travel, so there's nothing left to negotiate once you land.</p>
