<p>The station is really two connected buildings. The older structure, a nineteenth-century iron-and-glass train shed, was taken out of use for through-trains when a newer building, Puerta de Atocha, opened in 1992 to launch Spain's first AVE line. Rather than demolish the original shed, the renovation converted it into an extraordinary indoor space: a tropical garden of several hundred plant species growing under the original iron ribs and glass roof, complete with a pond that is home to turtles. It now functions as the station's atrium, ringed with cafés and seating, and it's worth a few minutes even if you're only passing through on your way to a platform.</p>
