<p>Atocha is Madrid's largest station and the hub for AVE high-speed trains arriving from the south and east — Toledo, Seville, Córdoba, Málaga, Alicante, and Valencia all connect here — which makes it the most common starting point in Madrid for travellers who've just finished a domestic leg of a longer trip. The station itself is split between the modern Puerta de Atocha building, used for AVE and long-distance arrivals, and the older nineteenth-century hall next door, now known for the striking indoor tropical garden built inside the original iron-and-glass train shed.</p>
