<p>Travellers arriving from another city by AVE are often carrying more luggage than a typical day trip, particularly if the Madrid stop is the midpoint of a longer holiday rather than its start or end. A private transfer handles that comfortably, with a driver on hand to help load bags at the station rather than leaving you to manage cases through a taxi queue. For families or small groups travelling together, it also avoids splitting up between multiple taxis, which matters more than it might seem when everyone needs to reach the same terminal by the same time.</p>
